Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Show the charge state on the NOTE4C power LED

A ULP-FSM program reads the charger status lines every 500 ms, also in
deep sleep, and drives the power LED (GPIO3, active LOW):

- GPIO2 LOW (charging): the LED blinks.
- GPIO1 HIGH (charge complete): the LED stays on.
- Else (on battery): the LED stays off.

The three pins stay in RTC mode, so ZectrixPower reads the charger
through zectrix_is_charging() and zectrix_is_charged(). The RTC
peripherals stay powered in deep sleep for the ULP.
---
 include/zectrix.h                     |  4 ++
 sdkconfigs/sdkconfig.defaults.zectrix |  5 ++
 src/power/power.cpp                   | 16 ++---
 src/zectrix.cpp                       | 90 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 4 files changed, 101 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/zectrix.h b/include/zectrix.h
index 1e70fb6..3d55021 100644
